# comp/common - what every agent shares

| Directory | Contents |
| --- | --- |
| `base/` | `odve_common_base_item.sv` - base sequence item (placeholder today). |
| `macro/` | `odve_macro.sv` - the framework macros: `` `odve_rand(obj) `` (calls `obj.user_randomize()`, since ModelSim SE has no constraint solver), `` `odve_cov_create(name) `` and `` `odve_cov_sample(name, args...) `` (functional coverage, below). |
| `cov/` | Functional-coverage runtime, compiled only with `FCOV=1`: `odve_cov_pkg.sv` (package-static counter store `odve_cov_store`, the base class `odve_cov_group` of the generated groups, the table lookups `find_bin()`/`find_trans()`) and `odve_cov_final.sv` (the one-line module that writes the dump at `final` - a package cannot hold a `final` block). `odve_cov_emu.sv` is the **emulation backend**: the same bins as synthesizable saturating counters with a one-hit-per-cycle sample port and an APB3 readback (counters at `4*i`, `NSAMPLES`/`N`/`W`/`CTRL` at `0xFFF0..0xFFFC`; `CTRL` bit0 freeze, bit1 clear) - always compilable, no `FCOV` needed; `odve_cov_emu_feed.sv` (FCOV only) mirrors every `hit()` of the store onto that port so a simulation can check the block, as the apb TB does with `+apb_slave=cov` and its readback sequence `odve_apb_cov_emu_seq`, which writes the run's `cov.dump` from the hardware counts (`# backend emu` in the header). `ut/` holds the SVUnit tests of the runtime (`make ut [VERILATOR=1]`). |
| `func/`, `pkg/` | Placeholders. |

## Functional coverage in three lines

Write the covergroup where the values are, in standard syntax, at package
scope, inside an `ODVE_COV_NATIVE` block; declare the group object as a class
property with `` `odve_cov_create ``; sample with `` `odve_cov_sample ``:

```systemverilog
`ifdef ODVE_COV_NATIVE
covergroup apb_cg with function sample(int len, bit dir);
    cp_len: coverpoint len { bins one = {1}; bins some = {[2:4]}; ignore_bins zero = {0}; }
    cp_dir: coverpoint dir { bins rd = {0}; bins wr = {1}; }
    x_len_dir: cross cp_len, cp_dir;
endgroup
`endif

class my_monitor extends uvm_monitor;
    `odve_cov_create(apb_cg)                        // -> odve_cov_pkg::odve_cov_apb_cg apb_cg_i = new("apb_cg");
    ...
    `odve_cov_sample(apb_cg, item.len, item.dir)   // -> apb_cg_i.sample(item.len, item.dir, NA, ...);
endclass
```

Without `FCOV=1` both macros expand to nothing and the block is never
compiled - the default build does not change. With `FCOV=1` the `acov` build
step (`script/cov/covgen.py scan`) parses the covergroups on the TB filelist
(`include` followed) and generates `build/cov/odve_cov_gen_classes.svh`; the
run writes `<RUN_DIR>/cov.dump`; `./regress.py <list> -cov` (or `make cov`)
turns the dumps into `cov/index.html`, `cov.html`, `cov.txt`, `cov.xml`
(UCIS) with per-bin test attribution, holes and the minimal test set;
`-ccov` adds the simulator's code coverage where it exists (Verilator).

Supported covergroup subset (the rest becomes a stub class that warns once at
run time - the build never breaks): `with function sample(<integral args>)`,
`coverpoint <arg> [iff (<arg>)]`, bins of values/ranges/`$`, `b[]` arrays,
`wildcard`, `ignore_bins`/`illegal_bins`, `default`, transitions
`(a => b => c)`, `option.at_least`/`weight`, `cross` with
`ignore_bins`/`illegal_bins` over `binsof()` (`&&`, `||`, `!`). Details,
rationale and the measured limits of both simulators: `odve/doc/fcov-plan.md`;
reference usage: `comp/agents/apb/vrf/tb/tests/read_test.sv`.
